                   NOTES FOR WINDOWS TERMINAL LIBRARY

1. In the present scheme, we force exit IMMEDIATELY if the etterm tolken is
seen. Is this correct ? What about if a "save file ?" dialog is to be
put up ? What does windows do, and why do windows seem to disappear before
the program acknowledges it ?
All this would seem to imply that there is no real way to stop a runaway
program from itself. That job ultimately belongs to the OS.

2. Why does the editor not use the same colors as the console version ?

3. Implement underline fonting.

4. Try a bold font, and see if that changes character width.

5. See about creating a separate thread to handle windows management. Care must
be taken about redraws.

6. See what happens when console mode is used on program.

7. Make sum fun programs. A clock. The snake game. Space invaders.
Whatever.

8. Need to refuse to make a window greater than 80x25.

9. Need to add scrolling controls to windows less than 80x25.

10. Need to teleport the window to the current text entry point.

11. Problem killing timers in windows. See bug1.pas

12. Killing programs via the "close" button (upper right) causes
programs to close but remain on the task list.
